  "light-and-blow": {"prompt":"TASK & FORMAT\nReplace the selected intermediate targets with the final photos. Preserve the 1080:1920 frame and the 10.37-second sequence.\n\nREFERENCES\n@video1 = finished video from pass 1; authority for timing, movement, camera and spatial staging, environment and lighting.\n@image1 = final appearance for Performer 1. Replace the intermediate subject identified as: The single centered performer, now in a full red hooded bodysuit with a white angular S emblem on the chest, holding the thin candle in the lips and later the cake, with the same timing and framing.\n@image2 = final appearance for Object 2. Replace the intermediate subject identified as: The cake held at chest height in the performer's left hand from about 5.9s, now a dark heart-shaped cake with red flower trim, receiving the thin candle in its top.\n\nTIMELINE\n0.0–0.5s: candle held in lips, unlit. 0.5–1.0s: lighter rises and ignites. 1.0–2.4s: candle tip is lit. 2.4–4.4s: lighter lowered, slow head tilt with lit candle in lips. 4.4–5.4s: candle drawn from the lips. About 5.4s: red flare transition. 5.9–6.4s: candle inserted into the cake. 6.4–7.4s: direct gaze to camera. 7.4–8.3s: smile. 8.3–9.3s: blows out the candle. 9.3–10.37s: final smile to camera holding the cake.\n\nMOTION & INTERACTIONS\nPerformer 1 (@image1): 0.0–0.5s: stands centered facing camera, head level, a thin unlit candle held between the lips angled toward frame left, hands down. 0.5–1.0s: right hand rises from frame left holding a lighter; the flame ignites at about 0.9s and is brought to the candle tip. 1.0–2.4s: holds the flame at the tip, eyes lowered to the flame, head tilting slightly to the right; the candle catches. 2.4–4.4s: lowers the lighter, keeps the lit candle in the lips held by gloved fingers, eyelids half closed, head slowly tilting further to the right and down. 4.4–5.4s: fingers close around the candle near the mouth and draw it away from the lips. About 5.4s: red light flare transition sweeps across frame. 5.9–6.4s: holds the cake low at chest level in the left hand and, gazing down, pushes the lit candle vertically into the top of the cake with the right hand. 6.4–7.4s: releases the candle, lifts gaze to the camera with a calm direct look while the cake stays centered at chest height. 7.4–8.3s: brings the cake slightly forward and smiles warmly, head slightly tilting. 8.3–9.3s: purses the lips and blows a short breath at the flame; the flame goes out by about 9.3s. 9.3–10.37s: straightens, smiles at the camera holding the cake steadily at chest height, slight sway.\n\nObject 2 (@image2): Not visible 0.0–5.4s. Appears after the red flare at about 5.9s, resting on the flat palm of the performer's left hand at lower chest height, slightly tilted toward camera. 6.0–6.4s: the thin lit candle is pushed vertically into the center of the top surface and stays upright. 6.4–7.9s: held steady, centered in frame, lifted slightly toward camera. 7.9–8.8s: held still while the candle burns. 8.8–9.3s: remains steady as the flame is blown out; the candle stays in place, a faint wisp of smoke. 9.3–10.37s: held at chest height with the extinguished candle, slight forward drift, no deformation.\n\nCAMERA\nVertical 9:16 medium close-up at face height, near-static with gentle handheld drift and a slow push-in, shallow depth of field keeping the performer sharp and the background softly blurred. Moody desaturated grade with warm flame highlights. One stylized transition near 5.4s: a red light-leak flare streaks across frame and the shot resumes with the cake in hand; otherwise continuous framing.\n\nFACIAL PERFORMANCE\nPerformer 1: 0–5.4s eyes lowered toward the flame with half-closed lids and a calm, sultry expression, lips gently holding the candle. 5.9–6.4s gaze down at the cake. 6.4–7.4s steady, serious direct look into the lens. 7.4–8.3s warm closed-lip smile. 8.3–9.3s lips pursed for a short blow, eyes on the flame. 9.3–10.37s relaxed smile at the camera.\n\nAUDIO\nMinimal close-miked physical Foley only. One crisp lighter click and short flame ignition at about 0.9s. A faint soft candle-wick catch at about 1.5s. One brief whoosh with the red flare at 5.4s. A soft frosting press as the candle enters the cake at about 6.2s. One short breath blow at about 8.9s with a tiny flame puff-out at 9.2s. Let each sound decay naturally; near silence between events. No ambience bed, no music, no dialogue. No bubbling or gurgling.\n\nCONSTRAINTS\nReplace only the referenced targets. Take their full appearance from the assigned images, including identity, materials and proportions. Remove the input design of each replaced target. Treat a multi-view sheet as one design. Do not transfer the background, lighting or static poses from character, vehicle or object photos. Keep unselected people, vehicles and objects, shot order and camera. Follow the attached video for exact timing, trajectories, gestures, wheel movement, handling, contact, occlusion and relative spacing. Preserve interactions and synchronized effects. Adapt grips or anatomy only as needed while preserving contact timing. Keep the environment and lighting from the video. Use each image for its assigned subject only.","promptSha256":"54f9278781a36daa8a304b371ec4e699a9931a3ea52346572d492f4ef41fe377","sourcePromptAvailable":true,"sourceAuditStatus":"verified-2026-11-13","sourceRecordId":"01a1d315-ab45-710e-af09-a1661185adf0","sourceMediaId":"4RXyg9iOyd7qVmJItuGs676lRZcimglwBwhDkLJI","sourceTitle":"Light And Blow","sourceSlug":"light-and-blow","sourceModel":"wan_30_omni","sourceModelFamily":"wan_video","sourceAspect":"9:16","sourceMinFiles":2,"sourceGenerationSettings":{"seed":1307808000,"duration":0,"file_urls":[],"shot_type":"single","model_type":"wan_30_omni","resolution":"720P","aspect_ratio":"9:16","native_audio":true,"audio_setting":"auto","prompt_extend":true,"video_duration":10,"rendering_speed":"prime"}},
